# Executive-summary render artifacts — .qmd is the source of truth, renders are reproducible on demand
executive-summaries/*.html
executive-summaries/*.pdf

# Claude Code local/runtime state — per-machine, never committed (settings.local.json,
# scheduled_tasks.json, worktrees/, checkpoints/, etc.). Previously caught only by the
# user's global ignore + per-clone .git/info/exclude, so a fresh clone surfaced these as
# untracked noise. Shared project config (.claude/settings.json) stays committable via the
# negation — ignore the directory's contents, not the directory itself, so the negation works.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# Run logs the synced methodology tools write at the repo root (BL-57 P11, Session 259):
# methodology_dashboard.py, context_budget.py and quality_ratchet.py. Per-machine output, like
# dashboard.html above. Ignored, not tracked: a tracked history would dirty the tree at every
# Phase 0 dashboard run, and every commit of it would owe its own CHANGELOG.md entry.
dashboard_history.jsonl
.context-budget-history.jsonl
.quality-gates-results.json
